// PHASE 3: full plot recaps for Arc 1 (Episodes 1–10). Uses WIKI.merge("episodes", id, {plot:[...], notes:[...]})
// so the original entries in episodes.js stay untouched. Each plot part is {h, p[]}.

// ───────────────────────── EPISODE 1 ─────────────────────────
WIKI.merge("episodes","EP01",{
  plot:[
    {h:"Cold open: Ultra Space", p:[
      "On a steel platform floating in the void of [[location:ultra-space|Ultra Space]], a Beast Ball sits locked in a coil-ringed cradle while light drains out of it along fiber-optic lines into capacitor towers. A crate is stenciled LUMEN MERIDIAN — FIELD ASSET 04, with the tagline “Light, reimagined.” Two technicians in charcoal clean-suits watch the yield graph on a Rotom-enabled Panasonic Toughbook 40.",
      "The draw has been dropping for six hours, and now it has fallen eleven percent since shift change. The pulses stop. A hairline of white light splits the black polymer band on the ball, and [[pokemon:necrozma|Necrozma]] tears out of it, cracked like a windshield and starving.",
      "Its plates lock like hackles. Every LED on the platform bursts, and the stored light in the towers whips backward into it. It isn't enough, so Necrozma burns everything it has and rips a wound in Ultra Space, then throws itself through. The empty Beast Ball drags after it like a dog on a chain.",
      "The Toughbook flickers back on: ASSET 04 — CONTAINMENT LOST, recall beacon active, nearest facility HR-01, Hampton Roads, VA. “Somebody wake up Verane.” The POKÉMON: PRISM title card follows, then the Arc 1 card, STARFALL."
    ]},
    {h:"The Kealoha house, 5:52 PM", p:[
      "It is a cold Monday dusk in [[location:denbigh|Denbigh]], with the Kealoha house lit up and loud. [[character:dani|Dani]] stirs a pot of chili in navy scrubs after a twelve-hour shift, while [[character:nova|Nova]] sits at the island drawing a sketch of the Starter Reserve with a girl standing on the trail under a question mark. Her Encounter Day slot is 10:40 AM, and the family plans to leave at 9:45.",
      "[[character:koa|Koa]] roasts the sketch and predicts she'll get a Magikarp. [[character:lani|Lani]] skids in with a good-luck voice memo that she insists is legally binding, and extracts a pinky promise that Nova will FaceTime her every day from London.",
      "[[character:noa|Noa]] comes in from the job and gets his hand smacked with a wooden spoon for stealing cornbread. When Nova admits she's afraid nothing at the reserve will pick her, he passes along [[character:papa-k|Papa K]]'s line: the dark ain't nothing but the light taking a break, it just gets tired sometimes. His phone chirps a grid alert (a load spike near Jefferson Lab, then a dip), which he waves off as one of the new Lumen Meridian sensors crying wolf. On the Nest Hub, the muted news stutters for half a second, and nobody notices."
    ]},
    {h:"Nova's room and the blackout", p:[
      "At 9:31 PM Nova is on FaceTime with [[character:journee|Journee]], who has a first-wave Encounter slot at 9:20 and teases her about the outfit laid out for tomorrow: black Tech Fleece joggers, a hand-painted purple Carhartt WIP chore coat, and the Dunk Low “Next Nature.” Journee tells her to stop doubting herself. Pokémon love her, and that's her one thing, or three things counting drawing and talking.",
      "Dogs begin barking all down the street. The Hue Go lamp stutters, Journee's face freezes, and the router goes amber. Her string lights dim as if something is drinking them through a straw. Then the streetlights die one by one, walking toward the house like footsteps, and the one across the driveway flares white and pops. The whole house goes silent, and her phone won't boot.",
      "Terrified of the dark since childhood, Nova gropes along the shelf for the one thing that still works: the green Coleman lantern that Papa K gave her when she was six, after a night of storm outages. Holding it, she sees a point of light falling toward the trees behind the street and is certain, for no reason, that it is falling toward her."
    ]},
    {h:"Into the woods", p:[
      "A glow pulses between the trees like a heartbeat, and it looks like it's hurting. Dani can be heard in the dark hallway giving orders, and Nova tells her she's fine. She breathes the way Ms. Batiste taught the class to approach a nervous Pokémon, says “I'm gonna get in so much trouble,” and slips out the back door in her UGG slippers with her chore coat on inside out.",
      "A Hoothoot on the fence swivels its head to stare at the trees, then flies away from the woods. Nova follows the glow past the fort tree to a small crater in the roots of a loblolly pine. In it sits a scorched blue-and-gold Beast Ball with a melted black band at the seam. The pulse leans toward her lantern like a plant toward a window.",
      "The sky goes white, and a sound like every transformer in Virginia screaming at once builds overhead. Something black and gold tears out of the clouds and falls toward the woods, and Nova watches the glow of Jefferson Avenue and the Walmart and Lowe's signs get pulled into it as it comes. It lands fifty yards north with a crack that splits a water oak and sends every bird in the woods into the sky. Then the light goes out, and she hears something breathing like glass under pressure. It sounds like crying."
    ]},
    {h:"The grid response", p:[
      "In Truck 4417, [[character:noa|Noa]] and his crewmate Dez Pruitt watch the sky turn white over Denbigh. The Dominion dispatch screen shows 2,140 customers out, an auto-classified “transformer failure,” a load spike of 340 percent and then collapse, a sensor source tagged Lumen Meridian GridSense, and a note that a Lumen field team is requesting site access. The white dot at the center of the red circle is his own address, and Dez does a U-turn across Warwick Boulevard.",
      "At Lumen's facility HR-01 the beacon is smearing: location confidence slides from 0.4 km to 2.6 km, cause “local light field collapse.” The voice on the speaker is never shown. “We will not chase the beacon, Marisol. We will chase the hole.” He orders every GridSense node on the Peninsula pulled for flickers and drains, and someone sent to the site with a hi-vis vest and a clipboard. Lumen is, after all, very concerned about the outage."
    ]},
    {h:"The lantern", p:[
      "Following a trench through the woods, Nova finds [[pokemon:necrozma|Necrozma]] lying on its side in the mud, huge and black like obsidian, edged in thin gold, cracked everywhere. A wide crack across its chest shows a dying glow. It turns its head, and its eyes open cyan.",
      "She recognizes it from three slides in Batiste's Legendaries unit, and from Papa K's porch story about the Blinding One that ate the light out of lamps. “They say it wasn't evil. They say it was just hungry.” When she crouches to it, she gets her first bleed: pain everywhere, and a hunger with no bottom.",
      "Its eyes are on her lantern, and the yellow light bends toward its chest, but it has no strength to pull. Nova talks to it the way she does at the rescue, admits she's scared of the dark, and sets the Coleman in the mud in front of the crack. “It's yours.” The lantern pours into it and goes out. She stands in total darkness and doesn't run.",
      "A sliver of black crystal as long as her finger breaks off Necrozma's plate and glows cyan in the grass, and she picks it up. The Beast Ball in the crater clicks open and a red-white beam pulls Necrozma back inside. Nova carries the ball back and promises, “I won't open it. I won't make you do nothing.” She zips it into her hoodie pocket, pulls the scrunchie from her ponytail, and slides the shard into her hair where it holds. Koa's flashlight sweeps through the trees, and behind it come the amber strobes of her dad's truck. She has no idea what she is going to say."
    ]}
  ],
  notes:[
    "Time stamps: Nova's FaceTime with Journee starts around 9:31–9:32 PM, the streak falls at about 9:38 PM, and she is in the woods by 9:44 PM. The dispatch screen reads 9:46 PM. Canon puts the arrival at roughly 9:39 PM.",
    "Nova's phone in this episode is an iPhone 16 in Ultramarine. She gets the iPhone 17 Pro in Deep Blue with a Rotom Core at kickoff in Episode 3.",
    "The Beast Ball is already melted at the seam and Necrozma was never in the ball when it landed. It lies in the woods, and it is pulled back into the ball only at the end of the episode.",
    "The voice Marisol takes orders from is Dr. [[character:elias-verane|Elias Verane]]'s, but the episode never names or shows him. He is first seen in Episode 3.",
    "Noa says Dominion has been installing Lumen Meridian gear on everything. This is the first appearance of [[article:gridsense|GridSense]], whose role in the crash is explained much later."
  ]
});

// ───────────────────────── EPISODE 2 ─────────────────────────
WIKI.merge("episodes","EP02",{
  plot:[
    {h:"The lie in the woods", p:[
      "[[character:koa|Koa]] finds [[character:nova|Nova]] at the crater with Dad's yellow Maglite in his fist. His beam sweeps over the scorched ring, the trench, the split oak, and a long smooth dent in the clay glittering with tiny black flecks. Nova grabs the first thing she sees past his shoulder: the Dominion pole at the back property line, its crossarm snapped, its transformer gone, its top ten feet charred. The transformer blew, she says, and that was the flash.",
      "Koa, shaking, drags her away from what he thinks are live wires. He retrieves the dead Coleman from the mud, never looking at the dent again. He tells her Mama went into her room with a candle, found it empty, and nearly ran into the street in her socks."
    ]},
    {h:"Candles and a hug", p:[
      "In the candlelit kitchen [[character:dani|Dani]] doesn't yell, which is worse. She checks Nova over like triage, then pulls her into a hug. The Beast Ball presses between them, and Nova twists away so fast Dani's arms close on air (a flinch that is really the ball's own: HANDS, GET OFF). Dani's fear comes out as a speech about what she sees in the ER when kids think something is a good idea for five seconds.",
      "[[character:lani|Lani]] asks if it was a Pokémon, and Nova answers “No” too hard. When Dani points out the Coleman's batteries were new Saturday, Nova says she left it on all night last week. It's the first real lie she has ever told her mother, and it comes out easy, which scares her."
    ]},
    {h:"The man with the working iPad", p:[
      "Out front, [[character:noa|Noa]]'s truck lights flood the cul-de-sac. A man in a spotless navy Lumen Meridian jacket is talking to Noa and Dez: he needs to pull telemetry from the pole-mount because the unit is on the GridSense pilot. His floating iPad Pro works fine while every other screen on the street is dead. Dez says he has never met anyone concerned about an outage except the crews and the people sitting in the dark. The man smiles and says he is as concerned as they are.",
      "He looks past them at Nova on the steps, a flat glance like someone checking a gauge. Noa later sits beside her and admits the can didn't just blow: in nineteen years he has never seen one come off a crossarm like that, scorched on the inside, and no transformer makes a ditch like the one out back. His hand ruffles her hair directly over the shard."
    ]},
    {h:"The first dream", p:[
      "At 1:47 AM the power is still out and the Beast Ball sits in a gym bag under her bed, pulsing slower and heavier. Nova talks to it in the dark. She tells it her name means “new star,” that her mother picked it because one star was left outside the hospital window the morning she was born, and that it was the only light in the whole sky before it crashed.",
      "She falls asleep and dreams of a city of impossible needle towers, thousands of people on bridges with their faces turned up, and herself as a vast radiant creature pouring light onto them. Then hands from every tower tear it off in strips, the city goes dark tower by tower, and she is small, black, cracked, starving. The scene shifts to a windowless white room, a cradle, a sphere pressing in on all sides, gold-visored faces, and behind them a taller man with gray at his temples and a kind face, who lays a palm against the ball and says, “Easy now. Nobody here is going to hurt you.” The light starts draining again.",
      "She wakes at 4:12 AM crying, with the power surging back on around her. The fridge kicks on, the string lights come up, and her phone boots to 3 percent."
    ]},
    {h:"Dawn emergence", p:[
      "At about 7:09 AM the sun hits the gap under her bed and [[pokemon:necrozma|Necrozma]] bursts out of the Beast Ball and into her bedroom, seven feet ten with its head scraping the popcorn ceiling. It knocks over the Tertial lamp and clips the ceiling fan, which jerks to a dead stop and pops its light kit. It drains her string lights, then pushes against the window and drinks the sunrise, dimming the room and dropping her phone from 34 to 27 percent. For the first time its hum is steady instead of glass-under-pressure.",
      "Nova talks to it through the first shaky laugh (“You broke my fan”) until Lani knocks on the door. Nova throws herself against it and yells that she is naked and sleeping at the same time, a teenager thing, and Lani runs off to announce it. Necrozma sags, too tired to stand. It resists the ball (cage, cage), and Nova doesn't order it in. She says she is asking, not telling. It goes in because it can't do anything else, with its eyes on her until the light closes. She starts picking up her markers."
    ]},
    {h:"Breakfast, the news, the clip", p:[
      "Nova comes down in her Encounter Day fit with the shard in her ponytail instead of a scrunchie. She says it's an obsidian clip from a Goodwill lady, and Dani tells her not to lose it in the woods. On the Nest Hub, WAVY-TV 10 reports the Denbigh outage blamed on a single failed transformer, with Lumen Meridian quoted as saying equipment fault, no public risk, power restored at 4:10 AM. The reporter mentions phones that wouldn't power on and cars that wouldn't start. Behind her, a Lumen tech pinches something small and glittering out of the trench mud with tweezers.",
      "Koa notes the line about a power surge doesn't explain how his phone, which was off, got fried. Noa walks in dead on his feet and announces he is riding with them anyway."
    ]},
    {h:"Encounter Day", p:[
      "At Newport News Park, two Pidgey on the entrance sign explode into the air the instant the CR-V rolls past. Nova's backpack has pulsed 400-plus times on the ride. At the pavilion she sees [[character:boogie|Boogie]] with his new Growlithe, [[character:kennedy|Kennedy]] with her Riolu, and [[character:jax|Jax]] filming with his Pawmi on his shoulder. Pawmi sparks, stares at her bag, and bolts under the Krispy Kreme table. Boogie's Growlithe growls at her, and Kennedy's Riolu, eyes closed and aura nubs lifting, steps behind its trainer.",
      "Handler [[character:castillo|Dr. Luis Castillo]] and his Chansey, Blossom, meet her. Blossom, who has never refused anyone, takes a step back and hides behind his legs."
    ]},
    {h:"No one came", p:[
      "Inside the reserve, Castillo gives her a single League Poké Ball and the rules she can recite from [[character:batiste|Ms. Batiste]]'s class: let it choose you, the ball is the last step. On the trail an Eevee comes close enough to sniff a Nature Valley bar, then goes flat-eared and flees, whining. A Rockruff, Fletchling and Pichu sunning on a creek rock bolt as the Beast Ball pulses and sends a flick of irritation (a tk) out of her bag. A Poochyena, a Growlithe, two Pawmi and a Riolu all run, the Riolu backing away without turning its back.",
      "Deep on the trail the whole reserve goes silent. A [[species:dreepy|Dreepy]] hangs twelve feet over her head, looks through her at the ball, and flees faster than any of them, back toward the gate. Castillo mutters in Spanish and suggests they head back. “There is still a lot of trail.” “I don't think anybody's on it anymore.”"
    ]},
    {h:"Wren and the Dreepy", p:[
      "At the gate [[character:wren|Wren Callahan]] is waiting for her slot in an olive Barbour jacket, with the Dreepy already pressed against her neck. It came out of the trees before her slot and through the fence. Wren tells Nova, with nothing in her voice: “It came from where you were.” The Dreepy shivers, keens like wind across a bottle, and watches Nova's backpack until Castillo steers Wren to the check-in table."
    ]},
    {h:"Whispers", p:[
      "Lani asks what she got, and Nova holds up her empty hands and says “Not today, baby” and “fine” three times while Koa counts them. Noa holds her and says it's just tired, it'll come. Jax mutters to his camera that Pawmi ran from her and she came back with nothing, until Boogie tells him to turn it off. Kennedy, arms crossed, observes that a whole reserve of Pokémon and not one of them wants her.",
      "At a side table Castillo files an RSV-7 observation: 100 percent avoidance by every species, a Riolu reading her aura and retreating, a Dreepy fleeing before the others and then selecting the next participant, his own Chansey refusing proximity, the reserve silent. Twelve years in the work and he has never seen a whole population avoid one person. Her second slot is Thursday, February 4, at 2:15 PM. The form goes to the regional review queue."
    ]},
    {h:"The cheer-up tray", p:[
      "Driving home through the rain with Frankie Beverly & Maze on 103.7, Noa offers a Cook Out cheer-up tray (Big Double, Cajun fries, banana pudding shake), and Nova says she's not hungry. She has never once in her life turned down Cook Out. Koa murmurs that she has held that bag all day like it's going to run off, and she says it's her stuff."
    ]},
    {h:"“I could just give you to them”", p:[
      "That night, with towels over the blinds and her phone locked in the bathroom, Nova sits on her bedroom floor with the ball in her lap and the Coleman on its brightest setting. She lists everything the day cost her: Jax's inevitable post, Kennedy's look, Lani crying in the bathroom over a dragon, Journee texted eleven times and left on read. Then she says out loud that she could hand it to the League and everything would go back to normal.",
      "The ball goes still for three full seconds, with a bleed of something she hasn't felt from it yet: small, cold, waiting, like a dog at the pound watching someone walk past its cage. She grabs it and says she didn't mean it, that she won't give it to anyone."
    ]},
    {h:"The alert in New York", p:[
      "At 10:14 PM in a high-floor office with no sign on the door at Unova League HQ, [[character:voss|Adrienne Voss]] and her Metagross read two alerts that landed minutes apart: a Class 3 Ultra energy event over Newport News at 9:39 PM ET lasting 41 seconds, filed locally as a transformer failure, and Castillo's flagged RSV-7 from 9.1 km away. The system correlates them at 0.18 confidence. She says, “It's never point one eight,” and taps HOLD FOR REVIEW over DISMISS.",
      "She opens Nova's registration profile: school ID photo, honey streaks, PTL pending issue, starter none, first destination Galar, departs 02/05/2027. Behind her, reflected in the glass, the Metagross turns its head slightly south."
    ]},
    {h:"Tag", p:[
      "Nova falls asleep on her floor with the ball in her arms and a new sketch under her pencil: a huge black crystal shape crouched in the dark and a small girl with a lantern beside it, captioned “it's just tired.” For a second the ball's seam glows with light pushing out instead of in. She sleeps through the whole night for the first time in two days."
    ]}
  ],
  notes:[
    "Nova's first encounter with a dream of Necrozma's past (the city, the hands, the white room, the kind man) comes here. The man is not named, but his gray temples and warm voice match [[character:elias-verane|Dr. Elias Verane]] as he first appears in Episode 3.",
    "The Beast Ball pulse count Nova mentions on the ride (412 to 414) is the first time she uses counting to steady her breathing.",
    "Voss's alert shows the event time as 9:39 PM ET for 41 seconds, which fixes the canon arrival time used in later episodes.",
    "Castillo's form is RSV-7, which later episodes cite as the start of the URD thread. His Chansey is named Blossom.",
    "This episode does not show Wren's own encounter inside the reserve; the Dreepy came to her at the fence before her slot."
  ]
});

// ───────────────────────── EPISODE 3 ─────────────────────────
WIKI.merge("episodes","EP03",{
  plot:[
    {h:"Kickoff Day at CNU", p:[
      "The Freeman Center gym at Christopher Newport University has been turned into a League expo for the thirty-six students of the Hampton Roads cohort, with stations for PTL credentials, devices, field apparel, care kits, and the League Field Card. [[character:journee|Journee]]'s new Pichu zaps her ear every thirty seconds, and [[character:boogie|Boogie]]'s Growlithe has already stolen a bagel.",
      "Journee calls Nova out for leaving her on read eleven times. Nova blames embarrassment about the reserve, and Journee lets her have the out, which tells Nova she will push later. At the devices station a staffer swaps her iPhone 16 for an iPhone 17 Pro in Deep Blue, 256 GB, with a Rotom Core. It floats up out of her hand and bobs at eye level, and she hates that it floats. Then its battery starts dropping, 100 to 98 to 97, and she glances at her backpack and shoves the phone deep in her coat pocket."
    ]},
    {h:"Dr. Verane's speech", p:[
      "Nova's field jacket is black and League-issue with a woven ID patch (KEALOHA, N. — HAMPTON ROADS — UNOVA), and she already plans to paint it purple. A League official introduces one of the program's lead sponsors, the founder and CEO of Lumen Meridian, [[character:elias-verane|Dr. Elias Verane]].",
      "He is tall, early fifties, silver at the temples, in a charcoal Brioni suit with an open collar and a steel Grand Seiko, with a Porygon-Z glitching at his shoulder. He skips the podium and sits on the edge of the stage with his legs hanging off. In a soft French accent he says that at fourteen in Kalos he was lonely and light was the only thing that helped, and that the most precious things are not things we take but things we are given.",
      "A single tk sounds from Nova's backpack, and she gets a cold bleed, like a hand pressed flat against the glass of a sphere. His voice is the voice from the dream: “Easy now. Nobody here is going to hurt you.” She stays seated a beat too long, and Journee has to pull her up."
    ]},
    {h:"The handshake", p:[
      "Verane works the front row. [[character:jax|Jax]] films the handshake, [[character:kennedy|Kennedy]] gives one firm pump, and Boogie wipes powdered sugar on his Nuptse first. Then he reaches Nova. He asks what Novalee means, and when she says “New star,” he says, “Of course it does.” He doesn't let go of her hand right away.",
      "His eyes go to her hair. The gym lights catch the shard and throw a spray of cyan and violet across her forehead, and Porygon-Z's head stops rotating. “Your hair clip. Where on earth did you find it?” She says a thrift store on Jefferson and that it's obsidian. He says it catches the light so beautifully that it is almost as if it is holding it. “Go gently, Nova.” Porygon-Z lingers a half second on her hair before following him.",
      "Three rows back, [[character:dani|Dani]] calls the man smooth, and [[character:noa|Noa]] says his people were on their street Monday night. “Just seem like they everywhere all of a sudden.”"
    ]},
    {h:"The TikTok", p:[
      "That night Nova hand-paints her field jacket with Posca markers, purple prism lines up both sleeves and cyan along the seams, because if her hands stop she will think. The new phone won't hold a charge, sitting at 41 percent after two hours on the cable. Journee texts her a TikTok link: @JaxCatchesAll's clip of Pawmi bolting off his shoulder, captioned that every Pokémon in the reserve said NOPE. Nova's face is blurred, but the glowing clip isn't, and the video is at 48.2K likes and 1,904 comments.",
      "One comment, from an account called lumos.watch, asks if anyone else saw phones glitch in the background at 0:07. The account has no picture, no posts, no followers, and was created that day. She puts the phone face down, the Beast Ball pulses under her desk, and she keeps painting."
    ]},
    {h:"Second slot, second silence", p:[
      "On Thursday, February 4, her second slot runs twenty-two minutes and goes exactly like the first. At the gate Castillo asks, gently and only for her, whether anything is different at home or around her lately. She almost tells him. Instead she says she is just unlucky, and he tells her she will have chances in Galar, that sometimes the right one is somewhere else. Then he pulls out his tablet again."
    ]},
    {h:"Norfolk and the goodbyes", p:[
      "At Norfolk International on Friday, February 5, the jacket is no longer plain. It carries purple prism lines on both sleeves, cyan seams, and a tiny painted Coleman on the left cuff that only she will understand. The Beast Ball rides inside her backpack, wrapped in a Menchville PE shirt, in a zippered pencil pouch, in the laptop sleeve.",
      "Lani clings to her leg and Nova promises every day day. [[character:koa|Koa]] returns the eraser he stole Monday night, says “Draw with confidence,” then hugs her and says low, “Whatever's in that bag. Be careful with it.” Noa lifts her off the ground and tells her to send a picture of Big Ben. Dani recites the rules with her: FaceTime every night, check in daily, stay with the group, don't go anywhere alone at night, and if something is wrong, tell her. “If anything is wrong.” “Yes ma'am,” says Nova, a beat too long. Program chaperone Ms. T. Gaskins, a sixty-something woman in a green windbreaker and a Kangol cap, whistles the Galar group together for the American flight through Charlotte."
    ]},
    {h:"Over the Atlantic", p:[
      "On the 777 to Heathrow, in window seat 34A, Nova has the ball between her ankles under the seat. The phone drains from 100 percent at the Charlotte gate to 22. Jax snores beside her with a backwards neck pillow. In the dark cabin she gets a bleed of hunger and confinement, a cage in a box in the sky, and she breathes four in, four hold, four out, Batiste's trick. She lifts the window shade an inch on a sky packed with stars, and the pulse under her feet slows. She watches the stars until the sky turns gray."
    ]},
    {h:"Customs at Heathrow", p:[
      "At 7:41 AM on Saturday, February 6, Terminal 3's Pokémon and Controlled Species lane is forty kids deep. Nova lays her one League ball and her blank program balls on the scanner plate, and the screen shows seven gray empty outlines. Then the bag goes through the X-ray belt. Border Force officer Priya spots the container in the pencil pouch, Nova claims it is broken, and Priya sets the Beast Ball on the glowing plate.",
      "Nova whispers, “Please be still.” The scanner shows an unrecognized, non-standard shell with no registry record and no occupant, and classifies it EMPTY — DEFECTIVE CONTAINER, cleared, with a 0.4-second field fluctuation at 07:43:12 logged as likely sensor noise. For less than half a second every light at Desk 4 dims and snaps back. The officer offers to bin it, Nova snatches it back and says it was her grandpa's, and he says keep it safe. Jax, filming, asks about the ball for heritage content. Ms. Gaskins confiscates his Osmo Pocket until Central London."
    ]},
    {h:"Meeting Sora", p:[
      "In the arrivals hall her phone floats up with a FieldHub notice that her group partner has arrived: TAKEDA, Sora, Hachiōji, Tokyo, Kanto. He is leaning on a pillar under the Galar banner in Dark Grey Heather Nike Tech Fleece and Pegasus 41s, matte black Ray-Ban Meta Wayfarers on his face, his League jacket tied around his waist. A Rockruff chews his shoelace at his feet. He scans the crowd like a lighthouse and then looks right at her.",
      "[[character:sora|Sora]] has a little Atlanta in his voice. She rattles off her whole introduction in one breath. He gives her “Sora. Takeda. Tokyo,” and when she teases that is all he'll give her, he answers Hachiōji, west side, out by the mountains, and she says now they're even. “Bet.”",
      "Then Rockruff stands, the rock collar bristling, and growls at her backpack, backing against Sora's legs. Sora says Iwanko in Japanese and asks what's wrong, then looks at the dog, at Nova, and pushes the Metas up onto his forehead. “Aight. So what's in the bag?”"
    ]}
  ],
  notes:[
    "Verane's first on-screen appearance. He carries a Porygon-Z and wears a steel Grand Seiko, which later episodes tie to a gift from his late wife [[character:simone|Simone]].",
    "Nova gives Verane the same cover story she gave her mother: a thrift-store obsidian clip from Jefferson Avenue.",
    "The chaperone for the American flight is Ms. T. Gaskins, a one-episode character. [[character:batiste|Rachel Batiste]] does not arrive until Episode 9.",
    "The UK Border Force scanner reads the unchipped Beast Ball as an empty defective container, the rule that holds until the League URD chip is fitted in Episode 9.",
    "The Heathrow scanner timestamp and the 0.4-second fluctuation at 07:43:12 are the first of several brownouts that follow Necrozma through checkpoints."
  ]
});

// ───────────────────────── EPISODE 4 ─────────────────────────
WIKI.merge("episodes","EP04",{
  plot:[
    {h:"“What's in the bag?”", p:[
      "At Heathrow Terminal 3, [[character:nova|Nova]] answers [[character:sora|Sora]]'s question in a rush: it is her grandfather's old broken ball from his Navy days, sentimental, and it smells like metal and age, which Pokémon hate. Sora says Pokémon don't hate old balls. “These ones do.” “Which ones?” “...All of 'em.” He looks at the floating phone showing 8 percent, drops the Metas back over his eyes, and says he isn't going to argue with her about her grandpa. Iwanko walks on his far side the whole way to the Galar desk.",
      "League staffer Dev Asante, a South London arrivals officer in a Barbour vest, assigns them Group G-114 and the League Galar Student House on Argyle Street, King's Cross. The warden is Mrs. Pryce, he warns, and she is not playing. He reads out that Nova's FieldHub shows “no starter yet,” and Sora's head turns slightly."
    ]},
    {h:"Forty pounds for a battery", p:[
      "In WHSmith Nova buys an Anker PowerCore 20,000 mAh power bank for £39.99 on her Field Card without looking at the price, the first thing she has bought abroad. Sora, eating a Twirl, notes her phone was at 100 percent when she boarded the plane, as the program's Charlotte gate photo shows, and now it is at 7 after ten hours in airplane mode. “New batteries be weird.” “Nah, they don't.”"
    ]},
    {h:"The Piccadilly line", p:[
      "On the Tube a Yamper named Biscuit hides behind its owner's handbag the moment it sees Nova, and an ad for Lumen Meridian, “Powering Galar's Tomorrow,” cycles over the doors. Sora talks about Hachiōji (a mountain, a lot of old people, and his father's JDM import tuning shop, TAKEDA AUTO WORKS), and Nova mentions that her dad is a lineman. For a moment it is easy.",
      "He tells her his Starter Day story at the Tama Hills reserve: everyone else was walking slowly, he started running, Rockruff ran after him for twenty minutes and tackled him into a creek. He hasn't nicknamed it yet, and Iwanko is just the Japanese for Rockruff. When he asks about hers, the carriage lights over Nova's seat flicker, and a tiny readout in his left lens spikes and flattens. “Glasses buggin'.”"
    ]},
    {h:"Argyle Street and Gwilym", p:[
      "Nova draws a Corviknight taxi, a steel carriage slung under its talons, from memory in three lines, down to the man's green tie. Sora watches her draw something already gone and says, “Huh.” The Student House is a cream townhouse with a green League flag and a plaque. Behind the desk Mrs. Pryce hands over keys to Rooms 31 and 32 on the third floor, lays down the curfew, and points to a huge sleeping Snorlax named Gwilym: do not wake Gwilym.",
      "Gwilym opens one eye, looks at Nova's backpack, and rolls over to put its back to her. Mrs. Pryce says mildly that he has never done that."
    ]},
    {h:"Room 31", p:[
      "Her room has a window facing a brick light well four feet away, a single frosted ceiling light, and an IKEA Tertial desk lamp. The Beast Ball is barely pulsing after twenty-two hours with no sun, and the bleed is dull and gray: hunger so old it has stopped screaming. Nova promises to find it a window. She has packed Papa K's Coleman and an eight-pack of D batteries.",
      "In the family chat [[character:dani|Mom]] asks for a text the minute she has wifi, [[character:noa|Dad]] tells her to ask whether they know the queen (Koa: “dad it's a king now”), and a voice memo from [[character:lani|Lani]] asks whether the bird taxis are real and tells her to name any Pokémon she gets after her. Nova laughs and cries, and when Sora knocks she shoves the ball under her pillow."
    ]},
    {h:"Regent's Canal", p:[
      "Sora wants to explore the canal, and Nova takes her backpack, sketchbook and all. Along the towpath near Granary Square they pass a Snom on a narrowboat roof, a Wooloo on a leash, a Cramorant with a fish tail hanging from its beak, and a Skwovet stealing chips. Sora's Metas log each species on sight, and he hits five new logs in five minutes.",
      "Nova sits ten feet from the Skwovet and draws it, cheeks first. It hops toward her, then looks at her backpack, drops the chip, and bolts into a planter. In five seconds the whole towpath clears: Rookidee, Wooloo, Cramorant, Snom. Sora, fifty yards down chasing a Corvisquire, turns around, comes back, and sits a couple of feet from her. She shows him the drawing, and he says she got the cheeks right.",
      "A patch of sun breaks over the gasholders and the pull from the backpack is so strong she nearly stands. Her phone drops from 61 to 55 percent, and there is nowhere in the whole city to let it out. The clouds close. Sora sees the whole thing and says nothing."
    ]},
    {h:"A first check-in", p:[
      "Her FieldHub check-in shows the Field Card at $533.40 (about £420), with the previous Wednesday's $600 stipend and the next due Wednesday, February 10, plus a notice that there are no approved capture zones in Central London, with Epping Forest and Richmond Park by permit as the nearest. Sora, on a Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra in Titanium Black, is furious: eleven hours in the air and nothing to catch. Nova thanks him for sitting down."
    ]},
    {h:"Dusk", p:[
      "It gets dark by 4:47 PM, and the pulse is so slow she keeps losing it. She says it is jet lag. After she goes inside, Sora takes off the Metas and reads the inside readout: a flat energy line all day with eleven spikes (Heathrow, the Tube, the canal steps, each exactly where she was standing) and one more when the sun came out that ran off the top of the graph. He looks up at her window and says to Iwanko, in Japanese, “What is that thing?”"
    ]},
    {h:"Necrozma in Room 31", p:[
      "Nova wedges a chair under the doorknob and lights every light she has aimed at the bed: the desk lamp, the ceiling dome, the Coleman, her phone's flashlight. She begs the ball to come out and eat, not ordering it but asking. The seam flares and Necrozma unfolds into the tiny room, its head cracking the ceiling and its limb smashing the Tertial lamp. Every light in the room is drained, then the whole third floor goes dark, bulb after bulb down the hall, while other residents call out and Mrs. Pryce shouts about the fuses.",
      "A knock sounds on the door. Sora, low and calm: “Open the door.” Downstairs Gwilym wakes with a groan and starts up the stairs, with Mrs. Pryce shouting at him to stop. Nova tells Necrozma she will not let the boy touch it, opens the door eight inches, and Sora's Meta glow is the only light in the hall. Rockruff is frantic against the far wall. Sora looks over her head into the room and says, barely audible, “I know you.”",
      "His glasses start screaming. The HUD reads N?CR0Z#A at 41 percent, type PSY???, origin ████ SPACE, energy field overflow, local lux 0.8, device power draining. Necrozma flinches back and cracks the ceiling again, its eyes going white as a pressure builds, with a bleed of being scanned and measured like the man's hand on the glass. “TAKE 'EM OFF!” Sora rips them off, and the glow slides back to cyan."
    ]},
    {h:"The Japanese adapter", p:[
      "Mrs. Pryce's flashlight beam sweeps down the hall with Gwilym behind her. Sora steps into the room and shuts the door, explaining that if he stays in the hall she'll ask what's going on, and if he's inside she'll think they're the ones messing with the fuses. Necrozma, pressed into the corner and watching him, keeps its head tilted. He speaks to it quietly, the way he would to a spooked stray in his father's lot: she isn't lying to you, she drew the Skwovet anyway. In Japanese he adds that it's okay, she won't lie to it.",
      "On Mrs. Pryce's count of two, Necrozma dims deliberately, pulling the light inward, and goes into the ball. She opens the door on plaster dust, a smashed lamp, a hanging wardrobe door and a scorched, smoking frame. Sora takes all the blame: a hundred-volt Japanese adapter, plugged in with a power bank, on a two-forty grid. “It was a big bang.” The scorch mark: “Sparks.” Gwilym sniffs at the lump under the duvet and gets sent downstairs. Mrs. Pryce says the lamp, the ceiling and the frame will come off Sora's Field Card, not hers, and he says it's fair. She asks Nova if she is all right, because she looks like she has seen a ghost."
    ]},
    {h:"“It's Necrozma”", p:[
      "Twenty minutes later, with the power back and the plaster swept up, Sora comes in again with ten minutes before Pryce finishes in the basement. They trade the grandpa line, and then Nova says, barely audibly, “It's Necrozma.” Sora laughs once in disbelief: it was a slide in Kanto too. She tells him it fell Monday night behind her house, that it was hurt and crying, that she gave it her lantern, and that it eats light, which is why her phone dies and everything runs from her. He pieces together the spikes. When he asks who had it before, who is “some people,” she thinks of the dream and the man in the gym, and says, “I don't know yet.”",
      "Sora starts to say what it felt like when he saw it, then stops. “Nothing.” He says it the way she says she's fine. He pulls up the Barbican Conservatory on his phone: the second-biggest in London, all glass, quiet early Sunday, a service door that doesn't lock right (his cousin did a study abroad here). That's not breaking in, he says, that's getting there early. She says she didn't know him at the airport. “You don't know me now.” “Yeah, I do. You told Pryce it was your adapter.” For the first time since Monday night she isn't the only one who knows."
    ]}
  ],
  notes:[
    "Sora says Iwanko is just the Japanese name for Rockruff and he hasn't named it yet. Later episodes treat Iwanko as the name he uses.",
    "The Meta glasses' scan reads the ID N?CR0Z#A at 41 percent and shows a pattern match with eleven earlier anomaly logs, origin KEALOHA.N, the first time Sora's own tech connects the spikes to Nova.",
    "Sora's line “I know you” when he first sees Necrozma is the first hint of the link between Necrozma and the Cosmog that led him off Mt. Takao in 2019.",
    "Necrozma goes back into the ball on Sora's word, not just Nova's. This is the first time it responds to anyone but her.",
    "The Field Card balance on the FieldHub screen is $533.40 on the Saturday before the second stipend. Costs for the lamp, ceiling and door frame are to come from Sora's card. Neither episode shows the amount.",
    "Rooms 34 and 35 on the same floor are occupied by other program students, one American and one who speaks Korean."
  ]
});

// ───────────────────────── EPISODE 5 ─────────────────────────
WIKI.merge("episodes","EP05",{
  plot:[
    {h:"A FaceTime with a Legendary in the room", p:[
      "On Saturday night, February 6, Room 31 has a strip of blue painter's tape over the ceiling crack with a Post-it that reads DO NOT TOUCH — M.P. [[character:nova|Nova]] has put the Beast Ball in the far corner wrapped in her PE shirt, and she begs it to be still as a rock before [[character:dani|Dani]]'s call. Dani asks why it's so dark, whether that is Papa K's lantern, and whether Sora was in her room. Noa demands something British (“Say cheerio!”), Lani asks whether she has named a Pokémon after her yet, and Koa says from off-screen that Sora is her boyfriend.",
      "A tk sounds from the corner. A thin line of red-white light leaks under the PE shirt, and [[pokemon:necrozma|Necrozma]] comes out of the ball on its own, slowly and carefully for the first time, bowing its blade-head under the taped ceiling crack. It fixes on the bright screen. Nova keeps her face still and blurts out nonsense to her mother (“Lani's school?” “It's Saturday, Novalee.”) while the phone drops from 71 to 64 percent and Dani's image pixelates.",
      "She reaches back, blind, and lays her palm flat on the plate of its shoulder. It goes completely still. She tells her mother the wifi is terrible and that she'll lose her, and Dani makes her repeat the rule: if anything's wrong, I'll tell you. Behind Nova the crystal hums, waiting. After the call ends she holds out the phone, screen up, and says it can have it. It takes seven minutes, from 58 percent down to 1, with the crack in its chest going gold. Then it doesn't go back into the ball. It settles into the corner beside the Coleman and sleeps in the open, and Nova sleeps without dreaming."
    ]},
    {h:"5 AM", p:[
      "At 5:00 AM Sora texts on WhatsApp: the front door unlocks at six on a timer, sunrise is at 7:33, the Barbican is thirty minutes' walk, and wear black. Nova texts that it slept outside the ball next to her lantern, and he types, “...deadass?” She dresses in black from beanie to Dunks, slides the shard into her hair, and asks Necrozma to go into the ball for thirty minutes in exchange for glass, plants and the sunrise: “No cage. No lab. Just sun.” It lowers its glow and goes in because she asked."
    ]},
    {h:"Walking to the Barbican", p:[
      "Argyle Street at 6:05 is empty except for a real fox trotting off with a McDonald's bag. Sora has mapped the whole route (Gray's Inn Road, Clerkenwell, Aldersgate, then the highwalk) after two hours on the map, and Iwanko wears a black Ruffwear harness he brought from Tokyo. Nova tells him about the FaceTime: she put her hand on it, and it stopped and waited. He says quietly that it slept next to the thing she gave it the first night. They pass a Nickit at the lake, which sees her and vanishes into the reeds."
    ]},
    {h:"The Conservatory", p:[
      "A steel staff door on the Barbican's lower level has been propped open with a cheap orange doorstop and a crushed Monster can: the cleaners' smoke break, per Sora's cousin. Nova says it is definitely breaking in, he says the door's open, and she goes through. Past a service stairwell and a fire door, the Conservatory is a concrete-ruin jungle: palms, ferns, banana and fig trees, ponds below, a roof of hundreds of glass panes.",
      "A Chewtle shoves a terrapin off a rock and snaps at nothing. Nova scans it with her phone's Rotom Pokédex, which flags sensor interference, and the Chewtle looks past her at her backpack and slides into the pond. At 7:27 they climb to the top balcony under the glass, and she sets the ball down and says it can come out if it wants."
    ]},
    {h:"Necrozma drinks the sun", p:[
      "Necrozma rises to its full height under the glass and looks up at a clearing stripe of pink sky. At 7:33 the sun hits the roof and every pane catches fire, and the sunlight in the whole conservatory bends toward the balcony. It drinks, its crack going gold and then white, its hum clear and resonant. For the first time its prisms turn, angling and throwing some of the light back out. Hundreds of rainbows scatter across the leaves, the concrete and the ponds, and the koi swim up toward the colors.",
      "The bleed is warm and full, so full it hurts, like the first breath after a week underwater. The shard in her hair blazes, and Necrozma looks down at it for a long moment, then turns its prisms a little further. Nova cries.",
      "Sora stands at the railing with his hands gripping the rail and his glasses off. A memory arrives: Mt. Takao, Hachiōji, August 12, 2019. An eight-year-old in a too-big Nike windbreaker and dead light-up Skechers, off the trail under cedars and a sky full of Perseids, crying for his father. A small floating light, deep blue and violet speckled with white, hums and chimes in front of him, drifts away and waits, and he follows. He says in Japanese, nearly inaudibly, “Why does it feel the same?” Iwanko, who has avoided Nova all week, walks to Necrozma and sits in the spill of rainbows, and Nova whispers that Iwanko isn't scared."
    ]},
    {h:"Lucien and the Absol", p:[
      "After almost four minutes Iwanko growls toward the far staircase, and a white Absol is standing there watching Necrozma. Behind it comes a boy of about sixteen, tall and freckled with loose dark curls, in a black Stone Island jacket, Corteiz cargos and Salomon XT-6s, with a woman's ring on a chain at his chest. “You lot do know this place don't open till eleven, yeah?” His eyes go to the Beast Ball and every drop of color leaves his face.",
      "Necrozma snaps its prisms shut at the sight of him. It smells him, with a bleed of lab smell: metal, cold rooms, gloved hands. Panes of glass overhead crack in hairline lines, and the Absol plants itself between its trainer and the thing about to go off, then retreats when [[character:lucien|Lucien]] orders it back in French. Nova walks toward Necrozma, not away, and tells it he isn't them, he isn't in that room, look at the sun. It goes into the ball on her word, without a recall, and Lucien notices she never used the ball.",
      "Nova's phone auto-scans the Absol (“If an Absol stops and stares at you, pay attention”). The owner field shows V█████, L. with no active PTL linked. Sora points out he has no license and Lucien replies that none of them has the right paperwork."
    ]},
    {h:"The fire door", p:[
      "A security guard shouts from below, and a Boltund called Sparky bounds up the stairs barking through crackling static. Lucien leads them through the Arid House (a Cacnea pretending to be a cactus closes its eyes at Nova's bag) to a fire door whose alarm has been dead since 2019. The Boltund sniffs the spot where the ball sat, whines, and backs away. They run out onto the highwalk to the lakeside terrace."
    ]},
    {h:"On the terrace", p:[
      "Iwanko sits against Nova's leg for the first time. Sora questions Lucien, who says he is Luc, comes here when he is in London because the Absol likes the quiet, and is from Peckham “mostly.” He says he isn't in the program, is sixteen, and has had the Absol since twelve when it was hit by a car on a hill in the Lake District. When Nova offers her hand, he holds it a half second too long and says her name means “new star” (Latin is close enough) and that his means light: Lux, his mum was big on names that meant something.",
      "He says he knows every glasshouse and east-facing roof in the city and offers a roof if she wants. Sora says no and Nova says yes at the same time. Lucien hands over his scratched iPhone 15 Pro in Natural Titanium, and she types in her number, just in case, despite Sora's head-shake. He whistles and a huge Corviknight drops between the towers. He mounts it with the Absol behind him and says, no longer smiling, “Don't let anybody scan that ball. Not the League. Not anyone. And don't let anyone take it off you. No matter how nice they are.” Sora says he doesn't like him. “He helped us.” “I know. That's why I don't like him.”"
    ]},
    {h:"What Lucien knows", p:[
      "On the Corviknight over Southwark, Lucien scrolls back through his camera roll to a photo taken through a window: a lab with a row of six brand-new blue-and-gold Beast Balls, each banded at the seam with black polymer. The metadata reads Lumen Meridian — Field Site Sherburn · 14 Aug 2025. He holds the phone against his chest beside his mother's ring and whispers in French, “What did you do, Dad?”"
    ]},
    {h:"Williamsburg, 3:02 AM", p:[
      "In his dark study in Williamsburg, Virginia, [[character:elias-verane|Verane]] reads a Lumen dashboard on his iPad: Lucien's iPhone 15 Pro, a light-field collapse at the Barbican Conservatory between 07:33 and 07:37 GMT (heaters, LEDs and glazing sensors down 94 percent), a signature match for ASSET 04 at 0.81, and a co-location flag with the two within 40 meters. “Of course it went to London. Where does a starving thing go? Toward glass.” His son's dot moves south over the Thames. “He always did like the Barbican. Simone used to take him on Sundays. He never knew I knew.”",
      "He texts a London number: pull all internal CCTV from the Barbican between seven and eight, quietly, and find every League field programme student housed within two miles, beginning with the Americans. Then he turns a face-down photo upright: a woman laughing on the Barbican lake terrace steps with a small boy of about four on her hip. “You see? He's helping me after all.”"
    ]}
  ],
  notes:[
    "The episode's last teaser calls Episode 6 “The Boy with the Name of Light” and says it opens with Ashby's call and a text from Lucien. The episode that actually follows is “First Mission! The Lights in the Cemetery,” and “The Boy with the Name of Light” becomes Episode 7.",
    "Lucien's line that Absol “show up before it” carries a double meaning. He knows what the ball is and that his father wants it back.",
    "Sora's Mt. Takao memory is shown on screen here for the first time. He tells Nova the full story in Episode 18.",
    "Lucien's photo (Field Site Sherburn, 14 Aug 2025, a row of six Beast Balls) is the first evidence that there were other balls besides the one Nova carries.",
    "Verane's Williamsburg time is 3:02 AM ET. The Barbican event is 07:33 GMT. The photograph of Simone on the Barbican steps establishes Sundays at the Barbican as a family habit.",
    "Lucien's name (from Latin lux, \"light\") is first tied to light by Lucien himself in this episode."
  ]
});

// ───────────────────────── EPISODE 6 ─────────────────────────
WIKI.merge("episodes","EP06",{
  plot:[
    {h:"The week before Highgate", p:[
      "Between Monday, February 8 and Wednesday, February 10, [[character:nova|Nova]] takes a call from her coordinator [[character:ashby|Ashby]], and a man in an overcoat is seen at a Pret asking about League kids. She buys an Argos ring light to keep [[pokemon:necrozma|Necrozma]]'s glow going, but on the failing-ring-light night its cracks worsen and her texts to \"Luc 🌙\" go unanswered.",
      "On Wednesday morning the FieldHub mission board lists a mandatory Ghost-type night survey at Highgate. Dani FaceTimes from the hospital break room, and Jax's Highgate TikTok sets up the cemetery as a viral spot."
    ]},
    {h:"Meeting Dr. Hale", p:[
      "At 4:52 PM [[character:nova|Nova]] and [[character:sora|Sora]] walk up Swain's Lane to the West Cemetery gate, where [[character:hale|Dr. Imogen Hale]] and her Dusclops are waiting. Nova talks nonstop out of nerves until Sora tells her \"You good. I'm right here.\" Sora's Metas cannot get a lock in low light, so he switches to his phone. [[pokemon:iwanko|Iwanko]] walks between the two of them."
    ]},
    {h:"The Egyptian Avenue", p:[
      "At 5:11 PM Hale leads them through the Egyptian Avenue, has Nova turn her Coleman lantern down to an ember, and switches off her own headtorch. Violet flames rise across the Circle of Lebanon. Nova's Rotom Pokédex identifies [[species:litwick|Litwick]] and warns \"Do not follow a Litwick in the dark.\" It estimates 40–60 individuals, and Hale counts 52, up from 31 in October."
    ]},
    {h:"The colony comes for Nova", p:[
      "The colony breaks its normal shy behavior and drifts straight at Nova. Dusclops looks at her backpack, and Nova realizes the colony is drawn to Necrozma, \"a hole in the light.\" Hale blocks the way, is drained, and collapses. Dusclops pulls in nine Litwick and sinks, spent. Nova is next: the cold starts inside her chest, her vision tunnels, and she drops to her knees as her Coleman is snuffed out.",
      "Sora commands Iwanko in his first real battle. Rock Throw scatters the front of the swarm. Tackle passes straight through a Ghost-type, a mistake Nova mumbles the answer to, and Sora corrects it with Bite."
    ]},
    {h:"Necrozma comes out", p:[
      "Necrozma tears out of Nova's JanSport, barely able to stand, and the Litwick see it for what it is: a mouth that eats light. The whole colony flees. Afterward, Nova finds the runt of the colony, a tiny, crooked Litwick with a nearly gray flame that never ran. Necrozma gives it the last of its own light, going fully dark for a moment before a faint flicker returns."
    ]},
    {h:"The catch", p:[
      "Nova offers the Litwick one of the blank program Poké Balls and it taps the ball itself. It wobbles three times and clicks. Sora's Metas had already logged the Litwick, so the catch is credited \"KEALOHA, N.\" and he laughs and cries about it: \"That was my Litwick.\" The [[article:beast-ball|Beast Ball]] rolls out of her torn bag and, for the first time since the blackout, gives a faint pulse."
    ]},
    {h:"Hale's report", p:[
      "Hale wakes and takes tea with four sugars from a dented flask. Sora covers with a story about a white flare over Waterlow Park, and a boy's voice shouting about a lightsaber from the far side of the wall backs him up. Hale does not accept it, but she decides not to ask: \"I'm not accusing you of anything... I write down what happens. And I don't write down what I haven't seen.\" Her parting line is \"Whatever it is you're looking after, make sure it's eating properly.\"",
      "FieldHub signs the mission off at 5:58 PM and pays £45.00 (+$57.15). Nova's League Field Card shows $1,115.18."
    ]},
    {h:"The viral flare", p:[
      "On the Northern line Sora shows Nova that Jax posted the clip as @JaxCatchesAll: a white column rising over the cemetery wall, 204K likes. One comment says the color at 0:03 is prismatic, and another from lumos.watch asks which students were inside. This is the same account that commented on her reserve video. Sora tells her not to post anything and to stay away from Jax."
    ]},
    {h:"Room 31", p:[
      "That night in Room 31 Nova releases the Litwick, a small, lopsided, eight-inch candle with a steady violet flame. It settles beside the shard clip, and its flame and the shard's cyan mix into silver-blue. She registers it in FieldHub as her first Pokémon and leaves the nickname empty.",
      "Necrozma comes out and the Litwick is afraid of it at first. Offered the Litwick's light, Necrozma turns away in embarrassment. The Litwick sits in front of its face without reaching, and a thread of violet light passes between them. Necrozma lets it happen."
    ]},
    {h:"Dani's call", p:[
      "At 10 PM the FaceTime call comes in and Dani sees that Nova looks better. Nova tells her family she caught a Pokémon. Dani, Noa, Lani and Koa crowd the screen. Lani demands it be named after her, Koa says a Magikarp would have been better, and Noa says \"It was just tired. It came,\" echoing his line about the dark. Nova sleeps on the floor between her two Pokémon, no longer afraid of the dark."
    ]},
    {h:"Voss's second flag", p:[
      "In New York, [[character:voss|Adrienne Voss]] receives Hale's report (GFR-2291) at 6:17 PM ET. It automatically links to the Newport News aperture and the Castillo reserve report, raising the common-subject confidence on Kealoha, N. from 0.18 to 0.61. She finds Jax's video, stops at 0:03, and sees a fringe of violet, cyan, gold and oil-on-water. She orders the Galar housing roster without logging the request, and leaves the Escalate button unclicked."
    ]},
    {h:"Tag", p:[
      "At 2:48 AM Nova sleeps on the floor beside Necrozma and the Litwick, with three lights and no dark. A text from Luc lights her lock screen: \"sorry. was out of town. found you a roof. 7am. bring your big lad.\" A FieldHub note from Ashby asks her to call in the morning. Necrozma watches the screen and then closes its eyes."
    ]}
  ],
  notes:[
    "Hale's report GFR-2291 times the dispersal at 17:21 and the Highgate visit at 17:05–17:35 GMT.",
    "The Litwick is Nova's first registered Pokémon, caught in a program Poké Ball (#PB-11873) under PTL-UNV-27-04418. Her guardian is listed as Danielle Kealoha.",
    "The Beast Ball pulses again only after Necrozma gives away its light to the runt Litwick.",
    "Sora's Metas logged the Litwick first, but FieldHub credits the catch to Kealoha, N.",
    "The Ep 6 closing teaser previews Ep 7 as \"The Boy with the Name of Light\", the English rendering of 光の名を持つ少年."
  ]
});

// ───────────────────────── EPISODE 7 ─────────────────────────
WIKI.merge("episodes","EP07",{
  plot:[
    {h:"6:14 AM", p:[
      "[[character:nova|Nova]] wakes on the floor of Room 31 beside [[pokemon:necrozma|Necrozma]], whose cracks are edged with gold again, and finds Luc's 2:48 AM text. The sky is clear for the first time in a week, with sunrise at 7:28 and cloud due by 10:00. She almost knocks on [[character:sora|Sora]]'s door, decides he would say no, and goes back in. She dresses, hides the Beast Ball in her Monarchs hoodie pocket, and asks Necrozma's permission to go. It lowers its head and returns to the ball, tired rather than reluctant.",
      "At 6:22 she texts Sora \"dont be mad\", explains the roof, and shares her live location for eight hours. The message is delivered but unread. She sneaks past Gwilym asleep in the foyer, and it opens one eye and rolls over."
    ]},
    {h:"The Corviknight", p:[
      "At 6:36 on Argyle Street, [[character:lucien|Lucien]] lands a Corviknight in front of her. Nova scans it and the Pokédex lists the owner as \"V█████, L.\" with the record restricted. Lucien deflects with \"Just Luc.\" She climbs on, the Absol steadies her from behind, and Lucien tells the Beast Ball, \"Yeah, I know, mate. I'm not thrilled either.\" The flight over London gives her the city at dawn: St Paul's, the Gherkin, the Shard, the Thames."
    ]},
    {h:"Shad Thames", p:[
      "At 7:04 they land on a scaffolded warehouse roof at Shad Thames with Tower Bridge in view. Lucien says he checked that nobody had been up there since November, then sits on the farthest northwest parapet with his back turned. Necrozma looks at him and starts to lock its prisms. He says, \"I'm not them. I know I smell like them. I'm not them.\"",
      "At 7:28 the sun clears the horizon and Necrozma absorbs real sunlight for the first time in days. Every crack fills with gold, and its gold edging returns bright and sharp. Nova sketches the scene and puts a small figure on a parapet in the corner. The Litwick looks up at the rainbows."
    ]},
    {h:"Simone", p:[
      "Lucien eventually asks whether Necrozma is all right, and Nova invites him to turn around. He tells her his mother used to take him to the Barbican on Sundays before it opened, to chase the Lotad while she read by the ponds. She died two years ago. Nova won't let \"it's alright\" stand: \"Your mama died. That's not alright.\" He agrees. The ring on his chain was hers, and her name was Simone, from Peckham. He deflects questions about his father (\"Works a lot. Science. Boring stuff.\").",
      "He slips when Nova mentions Newport News (\"I've heard of it\") and again when he says the ball was \"keyed to\" Necrozma, then covers with \"Documentaries.\""
    ]},
    {h:"\"Did he ever tell you his name?\"", p:[
      "Lucien quotes Nova's own Barbican words back to her and asks whether the man in her dreams ever gave his name. Nova connects the dream voice to Verane's handshake at kickoff, but doesn't say it. She tells him only that the man never said a name and had an accent, French she thinks. Lucien goes white, stands, and walks off: \"Loads of French people in science, Nova.\""
    ]},
    {h:"Sora arrives", p:[
      "Sora's messages come in (07:14–07:52): \"ARE YOU FOR REAL\", \"im 10 ft across the hall nova. TEN FEET\", \"london bridge station. running\", \"on tower bridge. i see the building\", \"dont move\". He climbs the scaffolding, tearing netting loose, while Lucien points out that there was a staircase in the core. Sora and Lucien clash (\"Don't call me mate.\" / \"Alright, bruv.\") until Nova steps between them. Necrozma hums at Sora, and Lucien says quietly, \"He likes you.\"",
      "Lucien leaves, thanks Nova \"for telling me about the dream,\" and says of the man \"I don't know yet.\" Sora then tells her he was not angry that she went, only that she went without him: \"I would've come... you're my group.\" They sit and watch the sun until the clouds arrive at 9:51, and at 9:58 Necrozma walks back and lowers its head."
    ]},
    {h:"Ashby's call", p:[
      "At 10:31 on Tower Bridge, Ashby calls from his Suffolk kitchen (5:32 AM ET) and congratulates Nova on the Litwick. He mentions that Hale's note says the colony was \"unusually attracted\" to her. Then he passes on a Lumen Meridian Education Partnerships \"Student Spotlight\" request for her lodging address and availability. Nova panics and asks him to decline, and Sora covers by calling them \"very private.\" Ashby agrees not to release anyone's address without consent.",
      "After the call Nova admits to Sora that she suspected Verane since the handshake, when he said the shard looked like it was \"holding\" the light. Sora points out that Verane now knows what she looks like and his company is asking for her address. The Beast Ball pulses hard with a cold bleed of a windowless room and a hand on glass."
    ]},
    {h:"Papa", p:[
      "At 11:09, on the rooftop of a Peckham car park, Lucien drafts two texts to his father (\"where were you on the 1st of february\" and \"do you know what necrozma is\") and deletes both, whispering in French \"Dis-moi que c'est pas toi.\" His father's unprompted text then arrives: \"Bonjour, mon fils. Tu manges bien?\", followed by a mention of Sundays at the Barbican and \"be careful who you trust.\" His father has never mentioned the Barbican before. The Absol presses its horn against the phone in his hand."
    ]}
  ],
  notes:[
    "Lucien's Corviknight is unlicensed as a taxi and its owner record shows only \"V█████, L.\"",
    "This is the first time Lucien describes his mother (Simone, from Peckham, died two years earlier) and the ring she left him.",
    "Nova's refusal to say Verane's name to Lucien is a deliberate choice, not an inability. She had suspected Verane since the Ep 3 handshake.",
    "Ashby's Lumen Meridian request is declined on Nova's behalf and no address is released.",
    "The Ep 7 closing teaser previews Ep 8 as 灰色のコートの男, \"The Man in the Gray Coat\"."
  ]
});

// ───────────────────────── EPISODE 8 ─────────────────────────
WIKI.merge("episodes","EP08",{
  plot:[
    {h:"The man at the front desk", p:[
      "At 11:47 AM on Thursday, February 11, [[character:nova|Nova]] and [[character:sora|Sora]] return to Argyle Street arguing about who to tell. Nova suggests her teacher [[character:batiste|Ms. Batiste]], a former Ranger who went quiet during the Ultra Space slides. Inside, Gwilym the Snorlax is awake and growling at a man in a charcoal overcoat talking to Mrs. Pryce.",
      "He introduces himself as Martin Crale of Lumen Meridian Education Partnerships. He knows both their names, their group number, Highgate, and the Litwick. He looks at Nova's shard clip \"one second too long.\" The Beast Ball pulses and Nova smells the same clean, cold metal as on Lucien. Her Litwick flares and Rockruff bristles. When Crale leans toward her hood, Gwilym stands up and roars, and Mrs. Pryce tells him it's his cue to leave."
    ]},
    {h:"The card", p:[
      "Crale leaves two cards, one on the front desk and one for Nova, with a handwritten note on the back: \"Novalee — We'd so love to hear your story. — M.\" Mrs. Pryce points out the pen was capped before he walked in. She tells them he was also on the steps Tuesday evening, asking another resident which rooms \"the Americans\" were in, and calling himself a journalist then. She logs it for the Galar office and offers: \"If it gets heavier than you can carry, you knock on my door.\"",
      "Outside, Crale checks his Pixel. A note logged his battery falling from 79% to 61% in four minutes while Nova was near. He texts a French number, +33 •• •• •• 17: \"Confirmed. She carries it on her person. The clip is a fragment... Suggest we let her come to us.\" The reply: \"Be patient, Martin. Hungry things come to the light.\""
    ]},
    {h:"Calling Ms. Batiste", p:[
      "In Room 31, with the door wedged shut, Sora tells Nova to call her teacher. She FaceTimes Batiste in her Newport News kitchen at 7:08 AM, a Staraptor on a perch behind her. Batiste says the blackout wasn't a transformer, that she saw the sky from her back porch, and then: \"Kealoha. Show me.\" As Nova tilts the phone to the Beast Ball, it jerks hard in her hands."
    ]},
    {h:"The Darkest Day", p:[
      "The curtain glows red. The sky over London is crimson and Galar particles fall like embers. Every phone in the building shrieks an emergency alert for spontaneous Dynamax activity nationwide. Downstairs Gwilym begins to Dynamax. Batiste tells Nova to keep what is in the ball inside it, then stays on the line in Nova's pocket.",
      "In the foyer Mrs. Pryce stands against the glowing Snorlax with his old Heavy Ball and talks him down: \"Gwilym. Cariad. Look at me.\" Gwilym fights the particles himself, and the recall beam finally catches. Nova presses her hands over her own pocket as the Beast Ball strains toward the same red light, and talks it down too."
    ]},
    {h:"King's Cross", p:[
      "Outside, a Gigantamax Corviknight circles St. Pancras, a taxi carriage hanging from its talon by one strap. Euston Road is wrecked: a Boltund, a Drednaw, burning cars, a red bus on its side. Its trainer, a Scottish taxi driver, screams for it. Batiste forbids Nova to act: \"You say yes before you hear the whole question... You are fourteen.\" When the strap snaps, Nova runs into the road anyway.",
      "[[character:lucien|Lucien]] dives in on his own Corviknight while the red particles try to take it over, shouts \"Reste avec moi!\", and catches the falling carriage. He recalls his Corviknight and says the Absol woke him at half past eleven. Then the Gigantamax Corviknight turns toward Nova, drawn by the Beast Ball. The Absol's Night Slash and Rockruff's Rock Throw do nothing to it."
    ]},
    {h:"Necrozma", p:[
      "The Beast Ball bursts open and [[pokemon:necrozma|Necrozma]], filled with Galar particles, rises in front of the Corviknight and begins charging Prismatic Laser. Nova steps under it, begs it not to fire, and tells it that is not who it was: \"You was the light! You gave it to a whole city!\" The star becomes an open hand. Necrozma pulls the red out of the Corviknight, which shrinks to normal size, and catches it with a psychic cushion. The driver sobs over his Corviknight, whose name is Arthur.",
      "Overloaded, Necrozma starts to crack. Nova tells it to give the energy back to the sky, and it fires a pillar of light that splits the cloud over King's Cross. Sunlight comes down on the Euston Road. The crowd applauds, then phone flashes go off. Necrozma panics, and Nova screams for them to stop. She talks it into the ball, still on Jax's TikTok LIVE (1.4 million viewers)."
    ]},
    {h:"Stay or run", p:[
      "Police and League officers close in. Lucien offers to fly Nova out and warns her about what happens once they have it in a room: \"I know.\" Nova asks how he knows and he can't say. She chooses to stay, and Sora stays with her. Lucien whispers \"Don't tell them about the man. Please,\" and flies away.",
      "A Met Police sergeant asks for the ball. Nova refuses, politely. Batiste, calling from a car on the way to Norfolk International, tells her to stay, keep the ball, and say nothing about its origin \"till I get there.\" Senior Field Officer Adaeze Okafor of the Galar Division arrives, claims League jurisdiction, and promises not to take the ball for now."
    ]},
    {h:"University College Hospital", p:[
      "At UCH A&E, Dr. Priya Shah treats the partial-thickness burn on Nova's right palm. The waiting-room TV announces that the Darkest Day is \"contained\" and shows footage of two large Pokémon near Birmingham. An unidentified Legendary at King's Cross is mentioned too.",
      "Nova FaceTimes the Kealoha family at 1:56 PM. Dani is furious and shaking, Noa guesses that the blackout was the creature, Koa says he knew something was off, and Lani asks whether it's nice. Nova answers yes. Lani tells her to name it Lani. Dani announces she is flying out Saturday and orders check-ins every four hours: \"I'm so mad at you I can't see straight. And you did good.\""
    ]},
    {h:"Voss", p:[
      "At 9:47 PM in Conference Room 4B of the League's Galar Division office at 5 Pancras Square, Nova waits with Sora, Okafor, and the Litwick. [[character:voss|Adrienne Voss]] arrives with her Metagross. The Litwick, which has learned Smog from the day's smoke, hides the Beast Ball in a cloud and faces down the Metagross, which parts the smoke with a psychic wave. Voss calls the Litwick brave, introduces herself as being with the Ultra Research Division, and says she has been looking for Nova since February 2. She slides a phone across the table showing a photo of the Denbigh sky on Monday night and asks: \"What did you find in the woods?\""
    ]}
  ],
  notes:[
    "Martin Crale first appears here. Mrs. Pryce's visitor-book entry records him as \"journalist\" on Feb 9 and \"Lumen Meridian\" on Feb 11, and the French contact he texts is unnamed.",
    "The Darkest Day is a nationwide Dynamax outbreak (Galar-wide red sky, Galar particles). The Ep 8 broadcasts confirm a column of energy near Birmingham and later \"two large Pokémon\" at the source. Necrozma's pillar over King's Cross is separate from that.",
    "Gwilym's Heavy Ball is old and scuffed. Mrs. Pryce says he hated being Dynamaxed in Cardiff.",
    "Necrozma uses a Prismatic Laser charge only to absorb and expel, never to fire at the Corviknight. This is its first on-camera appearance, streamed live by Jax to 1.4M viewers.",
    "The Litwick learns Smog on the day of the Darkest Day and uses it to shield the Beast Ball in front of Voss.",
    "Dani's visit is set for Saturday, which leads into Ep 10 (\"The Day Mom Came\"). The Ep 8 closing teaser previews Ep 9 as 見張られた星."
  ]
});

// ───────────────────────── EPISODE 9 ─────────────────────────
WIKI.merge("episodes","EP09",{
  plot:[
    {h:"Voss lays it out", p:[
      "At 9:51 PM on February 11, in Conference Room 4B, [[character:voss|Voss]] explains how she found [[character:nova|Nova]]: a rideshare driver's photo of the Denbigh sky posted to a local Facebook group, which she found on Feb 3 and took nine days to trace. Nova will say nothing until Ms. Batiste arrives, and Voss reveals that Batiste called her office at 7:34 AM Eastern, the first time they have spoken in eight years.",
      "She recites the chain of events anyway: the Class Three Ultra Wormhole at 9:39 PM ET on Feb 1 (41 seconds), the reserve flight of every Pokémon from one student, the Heathrow scan reading \"empty and defective\", the Barbican light collapse, Highgate, and the Euston Road. She says to Nova: \"That's Necrozma, Miss Kealoha. Isn't it.\" Nova's face answers for her."
    ]},
    {h:"The Beast Ball", p:[
      "Voss looks at the ball from across the table and identifies it as a [[article:beast-ball|Beast Ball]], restricted equipment built to contain Ultra Space creatures. She says only the Aether Foundation's Alola facility makes them under League supervision, and \"They don't lose them... Not ever.\" The black polymer band on the seam is not Aether manufacture. Someone modified it and kept something inside. Nova won't say who. Voss orders the kids kept in the sixth-floor family room with nobody on her visitor list from the sponsors: \"Especially not the sponsors.\"",
      "At 1:48 AM in the family room, Dani's four-hour check-in arrives. Nova tells the ball she won't let Voss take it anywhere and says she is proud of it. A thin line of cyan appears in the seam."
    ]},
    {h:"Batiste arrives", p:[
      "At 8:34 AM on Friday, February 12, [[character:batiste|Batiste]] walks in with her Staraptor, straight off a middle seat at Heathrow, and hugs Nova until her feet leave the floor. She reveals that Dani called her at 2 AM and they talked for forty minutes. She sizes up Sora (\"he threw 'em\") and greets Voss with a flat \"Adrienne.\" The Staraptor and the Metagross stare each other down."
    ]},
    {h:"Conditional registration", p:[
      "Voss slides over League form URD-CR-1: Necrozma registered under Nova's PTL as her official starter, classified, under a conditional status. The conditions are a League telemetry chip within 24 hours, check-ins at 08:00 and 20:00, weekly URD-approved vet observation, daily natural light, no leaving the region without liaison approval, and no public release outside emergencies. Voss says she isn't taking it because it trusts Nova and nobody else, and that it is \"safer with her than it would be with us.\" Sora catches the sponsors remark and Voss spells out the Crale visit, the Pret question, and Lumen Meridian's Hampton Roads grid contracts.",
      "Batiste asks who else can see the chip's location. Voss says eleven people have URD clearance and she trusts nine of them. Batiste sets four terms: she signs as witness, she is present at the chipping with Voss's hands and Metagross out of the room, any vet must be one she approves, and Nova decides what she tells and when. Voss agrees to the first three and refuses to promise on the fourth: \"I won't push her. But I won't stop looking either.\""
    ]},
    {h:"\"What do you want?\"", p:[
      "Nova asks the ball what it wants. It shows her a picture rather than a bleed: her Coleman lantern in Room 31, turned down low, and her asleep on the floor beside it. She tells the room it wants to stay with her. She signs with her left hand (her right is bandaged) and Batiste signs as witness. Nova tells Voss, \"It's not for you.\""
    ]},
    {h:"Secure Technical Room 3", p:[
      "At 11:20 AM Nova is taken to a windowless white room with a grid of LED ceiling panels and a padded steel cradle, the same kind of room as her dreams. The Beast Ball bucks and the building's lights flicker. Batiste orders technician Rhys to turn off the lights and remove the cradle. Nova sits on the floor and insists the work be done with her holding the ball.",
      "Rhys cuts away the old black band, which is bagged as URD-0202 / Item 1 with a fingerprint baked into one end. Nova holds on through the surge and speaks to it throughout: \"They was taking. We giving.\" Rhys fits the new band with a green node, a flexible matte-black telemetry chip, and tells the ball, \"This one's different\" (his nan has a Lapras that hates its ball). FieldHub updates: Necrozma, official starter, classified, genderless, \"Unidentified Legendary\" to the public. Nova realizes she has been calling it \"him\" all week. Batiste says of the old Legendaries: \"They was here before anybody was handing out pronouns.\""
    ]},
    {h:"The roof terrace", p:[
      "At 12:04 PM on the eighth-floor terrace at 5 Pancras Square, Necrozma comes out for its daily light, which is condition four of the paper. It sees the new band and the green blinking node and feels another mark on the cage. As a patch of sun lands on the shard clip in Nova's hair, Nova offers to give it back. Necrozma lowers its head, then draws away and returns to feeding. It does not take the shard."
    ]},
    {h:"Verane watches", p:[
      "At 3:41 AM in his Williamsburg study, [[character:elias-verane|Dr. Elias Verane]] has watched the Euston Road footage for five hours, pausing on Nova's bandaged hand on Necrozma's chest: \"It listens to her... Twelve years of containment fields and recall protocols and conditioning, and it never once listened. And she just asked.\" He texts the +33 number: \"The League has her. Voss will chip the ball within the day. Let it happen. And find out everything about the teacher.\" On the side table is a photograph of a laughing woman at the Barbican lake terrace with a small dark-haired boy on her hip. He says of him, \"He was there, you know... He flew away. He always does.\""
    ]},
    {h:"Tag: the mirror", p:[
      "At 7:31 AM in Lumen Meridian's Facility HR-01 in Newport News, Operator One (Marisol) opens a feed she was told to open at 7:30 sharp: a mirrored League URD feed from source \"M.\" showing the new chip live at 1 Hz, ±3 m, on the roof of 5 Pancras Square, with the original band listed as in URD evidence. She reports to a superior: \"We watch. We don't touch.\""
    ]}
  ],
  notes:[
    "Voss states the Class Three aperture timestamp as 9:39 PM ET, 41 seconds, matching her Ep 2 flag.",
    "The Beast Ball's black polymer band is explicitly non-Aether and was modified by someone with access to Aether equipment and Ultra Space. Its fingerprint evidence feeds Ep 10.",
    "Form URD-CR-1 is issued Feb 12 under case #URD-0202. Its 'twice-daily' check-in is 08:00/20:00 local.",
    "The photograph on Verane's side table shows the small boy Verane calls \"he\" and says flew away (Lucien). The scene does not name him.",
    "The Ep 9 tag shows the League's chip feed is mirrored to Lumen Meridian by a source \"M.\", likely Martin Crale (unconfirmed in text) or someone else inside URD.",
    "From this point the writing chat treats Necrozma as genderless. Earlier episodes use \"him/he\" for it in Nova's dialogue and bleeds, which the Ep 9 scene explicitly calls out as habit.",
    "The Ep 9 closing teaser previews Ep 10 as 母が来た日, \"The Day Mom Came\"."
  ]
});

// ───────────────────────── EPISODE 10 ─────────────────────────
WIKI.merge("episodes","EP10",{
  plot:[
    {h:"Heathrow", p:[
      "At 7:22 AM on Saturday, February 13, [[character:nova|Nova]] waits in Terminal 3 arrivals with [[character:sora|Sora]], Officer Okafor and plainclothes League staff. The Beast Ball's green chip node blinks against her ribs. Dani texts: \"Don't you run from me Novalee.\"",
      "[[character:dani|Dani]] comes through the doors in navy Figs scrubs under a North Face puffer, straight off a shift. She checks Nova's bandaged hand, asks if they used silver sulfadiazine, and then pulls her into a long hold. The Beast Ball pulses once against them and Dani says \"It's warm.\" She thanks Sora with both hands on his face, after getting him to admit there was never a Japanese adapter. Then she says she's not leaving the country until she has \"looked that thing in the face.\""
    ]},
    {h:"Dani meets Necrozma", p:[
      "At 10:47 AM on the eighth-floor roof terrace, in real sun, [[pokemon:necrozma|Necrozma]] comes out stronger, with its cracks full of light. Dani steps back once, then reads it like a patient: \"Those are fractures... Somebody did you bad.\" She says Nova does that too, says she's fine. She tells it she isn't mad at it, that Nova gave it her lantern, phone, sleep and hand, and asks it to look after her the way she looked after it. Necrozma lowers its head until it is level with her face and hums. Dani says \"It's polite.\" Voss's Metagross turns its eyes from the ball to Dani for the first time."
    ]},
    {h:"The fingerprint", p:[
      "At 2:16 PM in Conference Room 4B, technician Rhys reports a partial heat-fused thumbprint on the old band, matched at 0.87 confidence to Dr. Mireille Faure, Senior Researcher in Containment Engineering at Aether Foundation Europe's Lumiose Research Office, unreachable since Feb 3 and \"on leave.\" Aether HQ in Alola replies that no Beast Balls are unaccounted for. Voss says it was \"someone with an Aether badge.\"",
      "Nova notices that the print is a woman's, while the voice in her dreams belongs to a man. Voss announces she is flying to Lumiose on Monday for a joint Kalos investigation and wants G-114 along. Dani refuses outright. Voss argues home is not the safest place, since the chip is visible and Lumen Meridian holds the grid contract for her street. Dani then does something she never has: she asks Nova what she wants."
    ]},
    {h:"Lucien returns", p:[
      "A security call interrupts: a boy named Luc with no ID or phone, and an Absol that won't stop staring at the lift. Lucien enters in his torn jacket with a cut on his cheek and says he came to say goodbye. Voss has Okafor scan the Absol and, using URD clearance, unlocks the restricted owner record: Lucien Alexandre Verane, 16, guardian Elias Verane, CEO of Lumen Meridian, record restricted at his guardian's request on Mar 14, 2025. She tells no one what she saw, offers only that he is registered but has no PTL, and tells him to sit down and eat.",
      "Lucien says someone texted him something they couldn't have known and he threw his phone off Southwark Bridge at 2 AM. Nova asks if it was his dad and he says, \"I don't know yet.\" He says he is going to Lumiose to see something. Voss replies, \"What a coincidence. So am I.\""
    ]},
    {h:"Nova's answer", p:[
      "Nova tells her mother she doesn't want to go home. If she does, the people who hurt Necrozma will come to Denbigh and to Lani. It's her job now: \"I signed the paper... I don't quit on nothing.\" She wants to find out who hurt it, make sure it never happens again, and see the world and draw it (she has filled eleven sketchbook pages).",
      "Dani sets terms: she goes to Paris with Nova on the train Monday and flies home Tuesday night, Batiste goes the whole way, and Nova calls every four hours. She tells her to go and see the world and come back. Lucien watches them from the far end of the table, still with an untouched croissant."
    ]},
    {h:"The light that won't go out", p:[
      "At 11:47 PM in Room 31, Dani sleeps in her scrubs on the bed. Nova lies on the floor with her sketchbook at twelve pages and tells Necrozma they are going to France on Monday, to find the woman who touched its ball and who she was working for. She says she isn't ready to say the man's name out loud yet, and Necrozma answers with a soft \"tk.\" For the first time in her life, she switches off the Coleman. The room stays lit by Necrozma's cyan glow, which doesn't dim all night."
    ]},
    {h:"Tag: the Crestfield roof", p:[
      "At 12:03 AM on Sunday, February 14, Lucien sits on the roof of the Crestfield Hotel with the Absol and his Corviknight and watches the cyan glow in Nova's light well. He says in French that she turned off her lantern. Arc 1 ends here, and the closing teaser sets Ep 11 as 「ユーロスター、光の都へ」, the start of Arc 2: City of Light."
    ]}
  ],
  notes:[
    "Lucien's Absol was registered in 2023 in Cumbria, Galar, as a rescue, and his Corviknight in 2024. His date of birth is 7 Nov 2010 (turned 16 on Nov 7, 2026), and he has no active PTL.",
    "Voss sees Lucien's surname and says nothing. The Metagross clicks like a bolt sliding into place.",
    "Mireille Faure is a red herring in the writing chat's own framing: the print points to Aether but the dream voice is a man's.",
    "Dani's check-in rule is every four hours.",
    "Nova's Litwick still has no nickname as of the end of Arc 1. Lani wants it named Lani.",
    "Nova has still not said Verane's name aloud to anyone."
  ]
});

